id: pm-vcs-w3yi
title: Disambiguate parent object-fetch endpoints from nested objects repositories
description: "Served paths resolve among the candidates the caller may read, deepest catalogued first (7341b0d). A token granted only the parent therefore reaches the parent's objects/fetch endpoint at tenant/objects/fetch, and the answer does not depend on whether tenant/objects exists. A residual wire-layout ambiguity remains in two cases: a server without --auth (every candidate is in scope), and a token granted both tenant and tenant/objects. In both, the nested repository takes precedence at tenant/objects/fetch, so the parent's object-fetch endpoint is unreachable at that URL while the nested repository exists."
type: Issue
status: closed
priority: 2
tags: []
created_at: "2026-10-06T11:15:21.827Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-21T19:04:12.432Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-21T19:04:06.790Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-21T19:04:06.790Z"
author: codex-sol
estimated_minutes: 120
acceptance_criteria: "An explicit wire address or compatible negotiation makes parent fetchObjects and nested repository fetch reachable together; regression tests cover no-auth, parent-only, nested-only and multi-repository grants; unauthorized requests retain the fixed denial shape."
parent: pm-vcs-ttc0
repro_steps: "Serve repositories tenant and tenant/objects (a) without --auth, or (b) with one token granted read on both. Request POST /tenant/objects/fetch: it resolves to repository tenant/objects, endpoint fetch. HttpTransport.fetchObjects for the parent uses the same path, so the parent's object fetch is shadowed."
resolution: Delivered by the audit-linked mainline implementation.
expected_result: Disambiguate parent object-fetch endpoints from nested objects repositories.
actual_result: "Re-verified unchanged main 27e1d84671fa: delivery 1efdf4b3ca0d remains in main ancestry; engine/config.ts, test/composition-consumer.test.ts remain present."
