  "2026-10-15T19:28:42.717Z",codex-agent,"Plan: reserve a non-catalogable control segment for explicit repository endpoints, retain legacy suffix routing for existing clients, and negotiate new paths via advertisement so new clients can still use older servers. Preserve scope-before-catalogue resolution for legacy requests; prove both parent and nested fetches with open, parent-only, nested-only and combined grants."
  "2026-10-15T19:32:46.577Z",codex-agent,"Design: /<repository>/.pmvcs/<endpoint>, with optional HTTP explicit-endpoints negotiation and legacy aliases retaining scope-first deepest-catalogued resolution. Existing non-catalogable .pmvcs segment fences the namespace. Behavioral revert proof: reverting only splitServedPathCandidates to origin/main makes the new matrix fail (0 pass, 1 fail): explicit parent object fetch returns 404 instead of 200. Fixed matrix covers open, parent-only, nested-only, both and invalid grants; legacy nested history and parent-only access survive; reserved-name registration is refused."
  "2026-10-15T19:35:15.601Z",codex-agent,Linked pm test execution passed 1/1. Added a real older-peer direct object-fetch negotiation case and kept the existing legacy peer fixture honest by removing the new capability it does not implement. Project test-result tracking is disabled; results are recorded here.
  "2026-10-15T19:39:10.767Z",codex-agent,Final review tightened explicit-path framing so a double-leading-slash root spelling cannot alias the canonical root endpoint. The matrix now denies that spelling as well as invalid repository and endpoint names. The legacy compatibility and authorization selection remain unchanged.
  "2026-10-15T21:04:45.621Z",codex-agent,"Complete npm release check at e03471b passed 1541/1541 with zero fail/cancel/skip/todo and all-source per-file 100% coverage. Parent/nested endpoint and grant regressions, older-peer compatibility, packed Node/Bun clients and served-forge authorization checks passed. A full Bun-invoked retry is running after an unrelated existing erasure-setup refusal."
  "2026-10-15T21:35:28.292Z",codex-agent,"Delivery gates at e03471b: both complete npm and Bun release checks exited 0, each 1541/1541 with 0 fail/cancel/skip/todo and per-file 100% coverage across all 65 source files. Explicit parent/nested endpoints, all grant combinations, reserved-name refusal, legacy aliases and older-peer negotiation pass. Earlier unrelated erasure refusal is tracked in pm-vcs-simi. Final receipt changes only tracker evidence and self-host artifact. Release claim, keep in_progress."
  "2026-10-16T01:15:36.760Z",codex-agent,"Round 2: verified missingObjects/uploadObjects lack first-use endpoint negotiation. The audit also found lease, forge, fetch, push and publish bypass it on a fresh transport. Centralize the existing fetchObjects guard in roundTrip, excluding advertise to avoid recursion, retaining the cached false legacy result. Add real served HTTP tests for parent/nested object isolation, explicit request paths, one-time negotiation and legacy fallback. Current suffix routing only makes objects/fetch collide with nested history; missing/upload do not currently have standalone suffix aliases, so direct data misrouting for those two methods is not established."
  "2026-10-16T01:18:59.048Z",codex-agent,"Behavioural revert proof: node --test test/served-direct-transport.test.ts passes 6/6 with the fix (0 fail/skip/cancel/todo). Restoring only engine/http-transport.ts from head 306e62e makes the same six tests fail (0/6, exit 1): direct missingObjects/uploadObjects send legacy objects/missing and objects/upload without advertisement, rather than advertise then the explicit parent namespace; legacy cases also omit required initial negotiation. Restored the fix and the linked pm test run passes 7/7 across two commands. This proves first-use namespace negotiation, not existing parent/nested data corruption for missing/upload; those suffixes have no short alias today. Central roundTrip protection also covers fetch, push, publish, lease and both forge endpoints. Updated malformed forge/lease responders to advertise valid capabilities so their downstream refusal assertions remain exercised."
  "2026-10-16T01:19:46.705Z",codex-agent,"Additional guard-only revert proof: remove just the new roundTrip negotiation line (leaving all other source and tests unchanged), then run node --test --test-name-pattern='all other direct.*explicit' test/served-direct-transport.test.ts. Result: 0/1, exit 1, bad_request: The fetch request does not hold a well-formed ref and have list. The first direct parent fetchObjects request uses tenant/objects/fetch and the catalogued nested repository interprets it as a history fetch. Restoring the guard passes; updated focused refusal and direct-operation tests pass 17/17, zero fail/skip/cancel/todo. Next: commit source, tracker and regenerated selfhost.bundle, then run npm and Bun release gates at unchanged thresholds, including clean git identity environment."
  "2026-10-16T02:33:37.269Z",codex-agent,"Round 2 delivery results at implementation 58b36219a617424951449c6690667f31157088a9: npm run release:check and bun run release:check both exited 0, each with 1,560/1,560 tests, 0 failures/cancellations/skips/todo. Both used isolated HOME and GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null plus GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1. Unchanged thresholds: all 65 measured sources at 100% statements/branches/functions/lines, 0% duplication, 357 declarations documented. Native Node/Bun consumer and denial scenarios, TOON, stat-cache, committed self-host equality, production audit (0 vulnerabilities), identity, packing, changelog and release-attestation checks passed. Linked PM tests passed 7/7; focused refusal/direct checks passed 17/17. Both behavioural revert proofs are recorded above. Current missing/upload data misrouting was not reproduced; the verified gap is first-use namespace negotiation. Legacy peers intentionally retain their existing ambiguous aliases when explicit support is absent. No new PM CLI defects or out-of-scope findings. The final receipt changes only tracker evidence and the regenerated self-host snapshot; verify that snapshot at committed HEAD before pushing. Leave this item in progress for orchestrator verification; no thread replies or resolutions."
  "2026-10-21T19:03:37.529Z",codex-agent,"Tracker reconciliation authorized for the audited verdict FIXED-STALE. Re-verified unchanged main 27e1d84671fa: delivery 1efdf4b3ca0d remains in main ancestry; engine/config.ts, test/composition-consumer.test.ts remain present. Disambiguate parent object-fetch endpoints from nested objects repositories. [PR #114](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-vcs/pull/114) (1efdf4b) disambiguates parent object-fetch endpoints, suppresses HTTP Date under Bun when requested, and fails closed on unreadable existing configuration; real transport regressions are committed. Scope: tracker state only; no new runtime certification or deployment claim."
